1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,300
I pray that with this day of beginnings, with a baptism,

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:10,400
that you will help us to know which direction to take our first steps

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:14,560
to bringing everything to you. In Jesus' name, amen.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:56,600
Well, good morning.

5
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:57,880
Good morning.

6
00:00:57,880 --> 00:01:01,980
So glad to see everyone this morning. If you haven't met me yet, my name is Ryan.

7
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:03,780
I have the privilege of being one of the pastors here.

8
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:07,900
I'm super excited for this day as we celebrate baptisms.

9
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:10,260
Baptism is a huge deal for us around here.

10
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:19,260
We get excited. We get to celebrate people making a decision to follow after Jesus with their lives.

11
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:21,820
And today's been a bit of a celebratory day,

12
00:01:21,820 --> 00:01:27,760
but I also know that some of you might come into the room this morning with heartache, grief, pain, suffering.

13
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:34,820
And I thought that song that we just sang was a perfect invitation to remember whether you're here and you're celebrating or whether you're here and you're suffering.

14
00:01:34,820 --> 00:01:37,980
There's a place for you at the table this morning.

15
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:42,560
I have two quick announcements before we hop into our message.

16
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:45,900
The first is an update on our parking lot fundraiser.

17
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:47,140
Some of you might be familiar.

18
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:51,160
We have planned to redo our entire parking lot,

19
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:55,900
and then we wanted to raise funds to do the parking lot for the kids club that we also use.

20
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:59,700
So we're loving our neighbor as ourself, but also we use it as much as they do.

21
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:02,700
So we thought it was important that we would take that on.

22
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:05,160
And so I started a fundraiser.

23
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:10,380
We originally had planned to just do the front of the parking lot of the kids club and leave the side alone.

24
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:14,820
And we needed to raise $18,000 to do the front of the parking lot.

25
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:19,900
And our membership asked us to go ahead and get a quote for the side of the parking lot as well.

26
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:24,220
And I think, I don't have the exact numbers in front of me, I think we ended up having, if we wanted to do both,

27
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:30,020
we haven't committed to do both, but if we wanted to do both, it was going to be around $25,000, somewhere around that.

28
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:35,900
You guys have been super generous and have got that campaign started off really well.

29
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:43,360
And this week I got a text from a friend of mine who was formerly, him and his wife were formerly a pastor of a fresh church.

30
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:45,900
Some of you used to go to a fresh church.

31
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:46,440
I know that.

32
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:47,500
We love a fresh church.

33
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,020
We partnered with them in a lot of ways.

34
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:53,640
And unfortunately they had to make the decision to close a little bit ago.

35
00:02:53,640 --> 00:03:00,500
And he texted me and he said, hey, you guys were such great partners to us when we were a church and we have some funds left.

36
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:03,400
And we want to give you $10,000 for your parking lot.

37
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:12,980
Which is just such a reminder of one of our core values, that we unite for the sake of the gospel,

38
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:16,520
that the kingdom of God in our city is so much bigger than what happens under our roof.

39
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:22,320
That there are churches all over our city right now that are meeting with the same purpose that we are meeting for.

40
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:24,320
And we don't do all the things the same way.

41
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:27,640
We don't agree on all of the finer points of theology.

42
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:35,480
But the thing that matters more than anything is that the kingdom of God has come through the death, resurrection of Jesus.

43
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:41,360
And we get to participate in that kingdom, cultivating that kingdom on earth.

44
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:43,620
And that doesn't happen alone.

45
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:44,840
We have to do that together.

46
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:48,040
And so I'm so thankful for a fresh church, for Sean, for Stephanie.

47
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:55,480
And for those of you that had previously given to a fresh church, your generosity continues to have an impact in our city.

48
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:56,940
And so I'm just so thankful for them.

49
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:59,900
I don't, again, I don't have the exact figures.

50
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:04,080
I think that pretty much gets us to the point where we're going to be able to do both parking lots.

51
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:08,300
We're going to finalize it this week so we know exactly where we're at.

52
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:09,420
But we're pretty much there.

53
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:11,220
So thank you so much for your generosity.

54
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:13,060
Yeah, that's great.

55
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:24,160
And I just love how God works because I'm, first of all, I'm not the type of person that likes to ask people for money.

56
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:30,900
And then to make it a parking lot, which is like a thing that you have to have, but it's not fun to be like, to pay for a parking lot.

57
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:33,860
And so I'm just, I love how God always provides for his people.

58
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:37,720
Secondly, we have Canvas Connection right after service.

59
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:40,220
It's going to start in the Kids Club from 1145.

60
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:41,800
It's going to start right at 1145.

61
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:45,340
It's going to go no longer than 1230, and I have refreshments for you.

62
00:04:45,340 --> 00:04:52,420
So if you are new or newer to Canvas and you just want to learn a little bit more or get connected with other people that are new in a room this big,

63
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:54,320
you might not know who's new, who's not new.

64
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:56,440
You might feel isolated or alone.

65
00:04:56,440 --> 00:05:00,960
This is really just a great opportunity for you to come and get to know people, ask questions about our church.

66
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:07,560
I will be there, and I will do my best to give you the brief synopsis of who we are as a church and allow you to ask questions.

67
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:12,260
It's going to be two weeks long, this week and next week, and so I'd love to have you join us.

68
00:05:12,260 --> 00:05:18,020
Maybe you've been coming to Canvas for a while, and you want to just see who's new and meet them and welcome them.

69
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:18,700
Come along.

70
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:19,740
We've got bagels.

71
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:20,860
It'll be fun.

72
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:21,840
Sound good?

73
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:23,300
All right.

74
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:33,520
So today, we are continuing a series we started last week called A Summer's Journey Through the Life and Ministry of the Apostle Paul,

75
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:35,800
who we know as Saul right now.

76
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:41,340
Barrett and Jason did an awesome job on our stage backdrop to emphasize this journey.

77
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:47,340
A lot of us will be traveling throughout the summer, and what we're going to learn as we look at Saul's life is Saul was always on the move.

78
00:05:47,340 --> 00:05:53,100
Reaching out to new churches, equipping the churches that he had started, he was always on the move.

79
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:55,400
So that's why we called it A Summer's Journey.

80
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:56,600
Last week, we started it.

81
00:05:56,600 --> 00:06:07,760
We said that Saul was a Jewish Pharisee from Tarsus, which was a Roman province northwest of Israel.

82
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:10,980
Sorry, I had to do the never eat soggy Wheaties in my head.

83
00:06:10,980 --> 00:06:14,820
Northwest of Jerusalem.

84
00:06:14,820 --> 00:06:22,900
He was educated in Jerusalem, so he was a very well-established Jew with a very strict doctrine of how to read and interpret the Old

85
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:27,340
Testament, but he also had a lot of interaction with Roman people.

86
00:06:27,340 --> 00:06:36,840
He probably worked as a tent maker before in his early life in Tarsus, and so he was constantly interacting with Roman people,

87
00:06:36,840 --> 00:06:38,660
listening to their philosophy, their religion.

88
00:06:38,660 --> 00:06:43,760
And so he had this really well-rounded idea of both the Jewish religion and the Roman ideology,

89
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:47,360
and ultimately that led him to persecute the church.

90
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:55,100
We looked at last week, he was a part of the first, of actively killing the first Christian martyr named Stephen.

91
00:06:55,100 --> 00:07:01,700
And he really just felt like the early church, the belief in Jesus as the Jewish Messiah was crazy,

92
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:05,780
and it was his job to make that stop.

93
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:07,720
So that's where we got to last week.

94
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:10,260
Let me pray, and then we'll get into our message this week.

95
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:10,600
Sound good?

96
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,600
Yeah.

97
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:13,500
Thank you.

98
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:14,580
I appreciate it.

99
00:07:14,580 --> 00:07:22,500
Oh, Heavenly Father, Abba, we love you so much.

100
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:25,800
We're so thankful for Jesus.

101
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,360
We're thankful for the kingdom of God.

102
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:30,420
We're thankful for this family that we have here as our church.

103
00:07:30,420 --> 00:07:34,740
And we just look forward to the opportunity to study your word this morning.

104
00:07:34,740 --> 00:07:37,920
We look forward to the opportunity to celebrate baptisms this morning.

105
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:42,020
And we just pray that you would be at work in all of our lives,

106
00:07:42,020 --> 00:07:46,220
equipping, encouraging, challenging, convicting.

107
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:48,700
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

108
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:49,180
Amen.

109
00:07:49,180 --> 00:07:55,720
Hey, I did forget to say, my message is going to focus somewhat on baptism, especially towards the end.

110
00:07:55,720 --> 00:08:00,280
And so we've got four or five people that have pre-planned, pre-decided to be baptized.

111
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:05,100
But I am going to do my best to preach the importance of baptism.

112
00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:07,380
And if you're in here, you've never made that decision.

113
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:10,400
You've never decided to follow Jesus through baptism.

114
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,500
The water's going to be open.

115
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:13,400
We've got clothes.

116
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:14,240
We've got towels.

117
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:17,700
And so I want you even now to be thinking, if that's not something you've decided yet,

118
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:20,740
what is holding you back from making that decision?

119
00:08:20,740 --> 00:08:24,940
And so I'd love to baptize more than the people we're planning on baptizing.

120
00:08:24,940 --> 00:08:28,680
So if you're in here and you're a believer, begin praying for those people right now,

121
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:33,440
that their hearts might be softened and that God might be drawing them to the waters of baptism this morning,

122
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:36,180
because there is a place at the table for each and every one of you.

123
00:08:36,180 --> 00:08:37,660
All right.

124
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:40,980
If you want to turn your Bibles to Acts chapter 9, that's where we're going to end up.

125
00:08:40,980 --> 00:08:46,000
A few weeks ago, Marissa and I got a couple babysitters lined up so that we could do a,

126
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:49,720
like our first big time away from Rory since he's been born.

127
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:51,760
And it was fun.

128
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:52,600
It was good.

129
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:55,400
We decided to go on a date to D.C.

130
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:58,740
There was a worship concert in D.C. in the evening we wanted to go to.

131
00:08:58,740 --> 00:09:00,740
And we're like, well, let's just spend the day in D.C.

132
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:01,780
We'll go to the Bible Museum.

133
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:03,500
We'll do some fun things.

134
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:04,200
It'll be great.

135
00:09:04,620 --> 00:09:09,020
And we quickly learned a lesson that we probably should have learned about 10 years ago.

136
00:09:09,020 --> 00:09:10,480
We've been married for about 10 years.

137
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:15,040
And that lesson is that we are not as adventurous as we thought we were.

138
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:20,560
I did all kinds of research and preparation.

139
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:23,040
I like to plan ahead on these things.

140
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:25,320
So I pre-reserved a parking spot.

141
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:27,600
I did all the research, all the street view maps.

142
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:29,260
I knew where we were going.

143
00:09:29,260 --> 00:09:31,160
I knew where we needed to be.

144
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:38,960
And about 0.2 seconds into the city, I realized that I had no clue where I was going or what

145
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:39,740
I was supposed to do.

146
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:43,160
And the way the GPS told me to go was different from, you know how this works, right?

147
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:49,400
And so throughout the day in the city, I just experienced three of my least favorite experiences

148
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:50,240
on planet Earth.

149
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:57,060
Number one, thinking that you know where you're going, only to realize that you are going in

150
00:09:57,060 --> 00:09:59,240
the opposite direction of where you need to be going.

151
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:04,460
Number two, realizing you're lost, having no clue where you are.

152
00:10:04,460 --> 00:10:10,360
What a terrible feeling, especially in a city far away that moves much faster than I, West

153
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:11,520
Virginia boy, like to move.

154
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:14,760
The pace of my life is just different than the pace of DC life.

155
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:16,360
Thank you.

156
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:17,020
Yeah.

157
00:10:17,020 --> 00:10:21,620
And then lastly, like as you realize that you don't know where you're at, looking around

158
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:25,960
at all of the people from the city and realizing that none of them want to stop their pace

159
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:28,160
of life to help you figure out where you need to go.

160
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:31,560
Like, isn't this, isn't this our experience in the city?

161
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:34,400
There's, there's really a couple of categories of people in the city.

162
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:37,620
There's people who know exactly where they're going and you are in their way.

163
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:43,640
There's people, tourists usually like me, who are confident that they think they know where

164
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:44,060
they're going.

165
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:45,900
And in reality, they don't.

166
00:10:45,900 --> 00:10:51,920
And then there are deer in headlight, lost people who know that they have no shot of getting

167
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:53,800
anyone in the city to stop and help them.

168
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:54,880
Does that make sense?

169
00:10:54,880 --> 00:11:02,420
So these are physical experiences that we have in our lives and it's tense and it's frustrating

170
00:11:02,420 --> 00:11:04,280
and it's confusing and it's difficult.

171
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:08,180
But I think if we're honest with ourselves, I think if we stop and think about it for a

172
00:11:08,180 --> 00:11:12,780
little bit, we, we also, we also often have these experiences spiritually.

173
00:11:12,780 --> 00:11:16,460
There are times that we think we know where we're going.

174
00:11:16,460 --> 00:11:19,340
We think we're headed in the right direction.

175
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:25,300
We think we're a good person that us and God are in a good place only to find out later

176
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:29,120
that maybe we were headed in a direction that God never asked us to go.

177
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:34,060
Oftentimes it takes us a while to realize that we're headed in the wrong direction.

178
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:37,080
And sometimes if you're in here and you're honest with yourself, spiritually speaking,

179
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:39,740
maybe you realize you're lost.

180
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:44,580
You realize you don't know where to go, but you're looking around for help and you don't

181
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:48,140
really see anybody that, that, that really actually wants to help you.

182
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:51,840
Maybe you've reached out a couple of times and the good Christian has said the right thing,

183
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:55,220
but they haven't actually stopped to guide you along the right path.

184
00:11:55,220 --> 00:12:00,420
And so as we, as we think about these experiences, I think we're going to see all of these experiences

185
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:02,560
in our story in Acts chapter nine.

186
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:07,440
And I just want to think about the direction of your life this morning.

187
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:13,160
Does the direction of your life align with God's intended plan for your life?

188
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:21,120
And if not, who in here, who might be able to help you kind of along the way?

189
00:12:21,780 --> 00:12:24,360
So Acts chapter nine is where we're going to pick up.

190
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:30,620
It's after Stephen's stoning, Saul launched a targeted attack on the early church in Jerusalem.

191
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:35,960
Remember his goal was to, to squash the growth of the church in Jerusalem.

192
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:42,740
And, um, Saul was pretty active in persecution and he was pretty successful at persecuting the

193
00:12:42,740 --> 00:12:43,000
church.

194
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:47,000
Um, the problem is how you define success, right?

195
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:51,120
Like he was pretty aggressive at persecuting the early church, but he didn't accomplish what

196
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:51,900
he had intended to.

197
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:58,600
See, he, he intended to accomplish crushing the church, stopping the movement, getting everybody

198
00:12:58,600 --> 00:12:59,980
to give up on Jesus.

199
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:02,900
But instead what he did is he pushed out these faithful believers.

200
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:07,860
He persecuted them outside of Jerusalem and they went into Samaria, into Judea, into the

201
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:08,700
surrounding areas.

202
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:12,720
And the church began to spread and the church began to grow more and more.

203
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:17,500
So the thing that Saul wanted to do, Saul wanted to stop the early church from growing.

204
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:18,840
He persecuted them.

205
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:22,080
And that persecution actually led to growth and expansion.

206
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:23,460
Isn't that like God?

207
00:13:23,460 --> 00:13:27,780
Nothing can stop the kingdom of God's growth.

208
00:13:27,780 --> 00:13:30,820
The kingdom of God is the only thing on earth that is eternal.

209
00:13:30,820 --> 00:13:36,500
And no matter how hard anyone tries to stop it, look throughout history, the amount of people

210
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:42,280
that have tried to stop the movement of Christianity and persecution only grows the church.

211
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:48,600
So Saul, desperate to accomplish his purposes, decides that if the church has gone out of

212
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:50,560
the city, then he is going to go out of the city.

213
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:53,420
He picks a city called Damascus.

214
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:59,780
He targets the city, I think on purpose because Damascus, um, it's a large, it's a city with

215
00:13:59,780 --> 00:14:01,080
a large Jewish population.

216
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:04,640
And it seems like from history that it had limited Roman oversight.

217
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:08,780
And so he picked this city where he thinks there's going to be a lot of Christians and not a

218
00:14:08,780 --> 00:14:10,880
lot of accountability or authority.

219
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:15,020
And he's going to go there and begin or continue his persecution of the church.

220
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:21,200
Acts chapter nine, verse one, but Saul still breathing threats and murder against the disciples

221
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:21,880
of the Lord.

222
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:27,540
He went to the high priest and he asked them for letters to the synagogues at Damascus so

223
00:14:27,540 --> 00:14:34,340
that if he found anyone belonging to the way men or women, he might bring them bound to Jerusalem.

224
00:14:34,340 --> 00:14:41,560
So Saul has decided that he is going to expand his persecution of the church.

225
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:47,060
And he's asking the high priest in Jerusalem to give him permission to go to the synagogues

226
00:14:47,060 --> 00:14:49,420
in Damascus so that he can continue his persecution.

227
00:14:49,420 --> 00:14:54,620
And the first thing that I want to point out in our passage today is the title of the people

228
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:56,600
that Saul is persecuting.

229
00:14:56,600 --> 00:15:01,620
Look with me in verse two, it says, uh, he's asking for letters to the synagogues at Damascus

230
00:15:01,620 --> 00:15:04,420
so that if he found anyone belonging to who?

231
00:15:04,420 --> 00:15:09,240
The way men or women, he might bound them in Jerusalem.

232
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:10,840
This is what I want to focus on first.

233
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:15,900
The title of the early church, the title of the early Christians was the way we weren't,

234
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:17,960
we weren't called Christians at first.

235
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:20,600
We were called followers of the way.

236
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:22,180
The term Christian came later.

237
00:15:22,180 --> 00:15:27,600
And what I think is so important about this is that the early Christians, they identified

238
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:31,680
themselves by the direction of their life.

239
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:39,300
Their identity wasn't rooted in an intellectual belief or a one-time profession of faith or earthly

240
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:40,780
political affiliation.

241
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:45,860
Rather, their identity was rooted in the direction of their lives.

242
00:15:45,860 --> 00:15:50,780
Saul doesn't care if a Jew intellectually agrees with Jesus being the Messiah.

243
00:15:50,780 --> 00:15:54,300
He cares if they are following the way of Jesus.

244
00:15:54,300 --> 00:16:04,940
So I think this is important for us to think about as American Christians because Christianity

245
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:10,020
in America has become a general category for people that don't necessarily identify as people

246
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:12,140
actively seeking to follow Jesus.

247
00:16:12,140 --> 00:16:14,680
Is that a fair assessment?

248
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:17,240
It's a general terminology.

249
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:22,500
The category has become so broad that it includes a large number of people who don't actually

250
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:25,260
desire to follow Jesus or obey him at all.

251
00:16:25,260 --> 00:16:29,100
They might intellectually agree with some of the truths in the Bible.

252
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:34,380
They might align politically with a group of people who call themselves Christian and vote a certain

253
00:16:34,380 --> 00:16:34,720
way.

254
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:38,020
They might have grown up going to church every once in a while.

255
00:16:38,020 --> 00:16:45,240
But at the end of the day, does their life, is our life, is your life identified by the direction

256
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:50,540
of your life or just some one-time profession of faith that you made, intellectual agreement that

257
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:53,260
you have with some ideas in the Bible?

258
00:16:54,760 --> 00:16:56,740
Barna did a survey recently.

259
00:16:56,740 --> 00:17:00,580
It's a really well-known Christian survey.

260
00:17:00,580 --> 00:17:07,920
And they found that 100—listen to this, this is crazy—176 million Americans.

261
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:11,560
We're like 330-some million, so that's pretty close.

262
00:17:11,720 --> 00:17:19,660
Like, that's a lot—176 million Americans self-identified as Christian, while only 15 million, throughout

263
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:24,920
the answers to their surveys, demonstrated an intentional pursuit in following and obeying

264
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:26,120
the teachings of Jesus.

265
00:17:26,120 --> 00:17:34,920
That's 8.5% of all self-identified Christians in America exhibit any pursuit of obedience to

266
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:36,480
the teachings of Jesus.

267
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:42,660
Christianity has become a term that we use for ourselves and for others, but does it mean

268
00:17:42,660 --> 00:17:43,980
what it meant to the early Christians?

269
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:52,260
If you're in here, you consider yourself a Christian, you would label yourself that way.

270
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:58,740
Does your life demonstrate an intentional desire to follow and obey the teachings and examples

271
00:17:58,740 --> 00:17:59,340
of Jesus?

272
00:17:59,340 --> 00:18:03,800
There was no other version of Christianity that existed in the first century.

273
00:18:04,280 --> 00:18:08,280
It was, we are followers of the way.

274
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:13,520
And they got persecuted for it, and they got pushed out of their city, and they continued

275
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:16,380
to follow the way because they believed the words that Jesus said.

276
00:18:16,380 --> 00:18:19,820
He said, I am the way, the truth, and the life.

277
00:18:19,820 --> 00:18:21,760
No one comes to the Father except through me.

278
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:26,440
And so if you wanted fellowship with the Father, you did whatever it took, you were okay with

279
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:30,100
persecution because you were a follower of the way.

280
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:39,060
So when we think about our Christian identity, I want us to consider, is it the direction

281
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:44,680
of our life, or is it more about some cultural identity, some political affiliation, or some

282
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:49,520
intellectual belief, one-time commitment of faith?

283
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:57,100
Here's a question that I don't know that I'm comfortable asking myself this morning, so we'll

284
00:18:57,100 --> 00:19:00,480
just ask all of you, and then I'll be tense together.

285
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:06,560
Listen to me, if Saul was persecuting followers of the way in the American church, would he

286
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:10,580
look at your life and my life and consider us to be a part of that group?

287
00:19:10,580 --> 00:19:13,200
Would he look at our lives?

288
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:15,240
We come to church on Sundays.

289
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:18,180
We have a Bible on our shelf.

290
00:19:18,180 --> 00:19:19,120
Maybe we read it.

291
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:20,100
Maybe we don't.

292
00:19:20,180 --> 00:19:25,740
If someone was persecuting followers of the way in our city, in our church, would he look

293
00:19:25,740 --> 00:19:26,360
at your life?

294
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:27,360
Would he look at my life?

295
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:29,100
And would he say, yeah, that's a target of mine?

296
00:19:29,100 --> 00:19:36,100
Let the Holy Spirit do whatever he wants to do with that in you and in me, all right?

297
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:42,140
So, first thing we want to point out, Saul, is persecuting followers of the way.

298
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:44,100
Now, there's a really stark contrast.

299
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:44,800
I love this here.

300
00:19:44,800 --> 00:19:50,000
It's not necessarily in the Greek, but I think the idea is there.

301
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:54,500
He says, he's on his way to persecuting followers of the way that he might bring them bound to

302
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:54,780
Jerusalem.

303
00:19:54,780 --> 00:19:55,400
Now, look at this.

304
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:55,840
Verse 3.

305
00:19:55,840 --> 00:20:04,580
Now he, Saul, went on his way, approaching Damascus, and suddenly a light from heaven shone

306
00:20:04,580 --> 00:20:05,600
around him.

307
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:11,480
See, I think there's a clear distinction here between followers of the way and Saul going

308
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:12,560
his way.

309
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:15,280
There's a very clear contrast here.

310
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:21,020
Followers of the way and Saul is going his way, and Saul thinks that his way is the way.

311
00:20:21,540 --> 00:20:26,180
Saul thinks that the direction of his life aligns with God's will for his life.

312
00:20:26,180 --> 00:20:31,520
He is confident and convinced that the things that he is doing is the things that he is supposed

313
00:20:31,520 --> 00:20:32,700
to be doing.

314
00:20:32,700 --> 00:20:38,300
And what he's going to realize very quickly is that he's actually headed in the very opposite

315
00:20:38,300 --> 00:20:39,900
direction that God has for him.

316
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:46,720
And this is a very, very clear picture of how all of humanity interacts with God.

317
00:20:47,980 --> 00:20:48,600
Listen to me.

318
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:52,800
There are only two spiritual directions that exist in humanity.

319
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:54,420
Only two.

320
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:59,900
There is the way, and there is my way.

321
00:20:59,900 --> 00:21:01,460
Your way.

322
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:02,240
Our way.

323
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:05,680
There are only two directions, spiritual directions in life.

324
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:10,400
We are either following the way that God has intended for us, or we are following our own

325
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:10,580
way.

326
00:21:10,580 --> 00:21:12,140
And that looks different for all of us.

327
00:21:12,360 --> 00:21:16,740
It looks like putting anything but God in the place of God in your life.

328
00:21:16,740 --> 00:21:19,260
But there are only two spiritual directions.

329
00:21:19,260 --> 00:21:26,400
You're either going with the flow that God has laid out for you, which ultimately is obedience

330
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:27,940
to him, submission to him.

331
00:21:27,940 --> 00:21:34,860
From the very beginning of creation, the fabric of creation was God as a loving father inviting

332
00:21:34,860 --> 00:21:42,360
us humanity, to just follow him, just steward creation in alignment with the way that he called

333
00:21:42,360 --> 00:21:42,700
us to.

334
00:21:42,700 --> 00:21:48,660
From the very beginning, there was rebellion, and that forged the road in the opposite direction.

335
00:21:48,660 --> 00:21:50,460
And from now on, there are only two roads.

336
00:21:50,460 --> 00:21:52,600
There is the way, and there is our way.

337
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:55,740
Proverbs 14.12 says,

338
00:21:55,740 --> 00:22:00,440
There is a way that appears to be right, but in the end, it leads to death.

339
00:22:00,440 --> 00:22:05,940
And I think so many of us are like Saul.

340
00:22:05,940 --> 00:22:08,540
We're headed in a direction, and we think we're doing right.

341
00:22:08,540 --> 00:22:09,280
We're good people.

342
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:10,460
We're doing the right things.

343
00:22:10,460 --> 00:22:12,280
We're prioritizing things that matter.

344
00:22:12,280 --> 00:22:16,800
But at the end of the day, if God isn't at the center of our lives, if we haven't submitted

345
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:22,940
our life to the leadership and lordship of Jesus, we're not heading in the direction that

346
00:22:22,940 --> 00:22:24,060
God intended for us to head.

347
00:22:25,740 --> 00:22:29,860
And that direction ultimately leads to our death and destruction.

348
00:22:29,860 --> 00:22:31,760
Matthew 7.

349
00:22:31,760 --> 00:22:37,940
Enter through the narrow gate, for wide is the gate, and broad is the way that leads to

350
00:22:37,940 --> 00:22:38,420
destruction.

351
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:47,160
And many will enter through it, but small is the gate, and narrow is the way, the way that

352
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:49,660
leads to life, and only few will find it.

353
00:22:49,660 --> 00:22:54,200
Jesus was very clear at the end of his very important sermon on the kingdom of God.

354
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:55,940
There are two spiritual directions.

355
00:22:55,940 --> 00:23:02,960
There is a wide road that many of us follow, and that wide road leads to our destruction.

356
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:09,520
There's a narrow road that leads to life, and only a few will find it.

357
00:23:11,420 --> 00:23:17,220
So, for you and for me, does the current trajectory of our life line up with God's intended direction?

358
00:23:17,220 --> 00:23:23,120
Are we walking in a way that seems right to us, but ultimately leads to destruction, or are

359
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:26,220
we walking the narrow road that leads to life?

360
00:23:26,220 --> 00:23:32,080
God's desire for you, ultimately, is that you would submit your life to him as both sovereign

361
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:33,740
king and creator.

362
00:23:33,860 --> 00:23:37,500
And look, here's the part that I missed for so long growing up in church.

363
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:39,800
I heard this gospel preached over and over and over again.

364
00:23:39,800 --> 00:23:43,340
I went to a good church with good people, but the thing that I missed, and I don't know if

365
00:23:43,340 --> 00:23:47,600
I missed it because of the way that they communicated or because of the way that I internalized who

366
00:23:47,600 --> 00:23:52,680
I thought God was, but the thing that I missed is that God is not a cosmic tyrant in the sky

367
00:23:52,680 --> 00:23:54,620
that demands your obedience or else.

368
00:23:54,620 --> 00:24:02,500
God is a loving father that knows the consequences of a life lived your own way.

369
00:24:02,500 --> 00:24:09,000
He's the creator, the sustainer, he's a loving father, and he sees us walking down this wide

370
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:10,280
road that leads to destruction.

371
00:24:10,280 --> 00:24:14,700
And he's not a cosmic tyrant in the sky saying, get it right or get out.

372
00:24:14,700 --> 00:24:19,400
He's a loving father inviting us to realize that we're headed down a path that leads to destruction.

373
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:22,020
We've got to get this.

374
00:24:22,020 --> 00:24:26,400
If we're going to be genuine followers of Jesus, we have to realize that the invitation

375
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:31,160
to follow him is an invitation from a loving father who wants us to experience life and

376
00:24:31,160 --> 00:24:32,140
life more abundantly.

377
00:24:32,140 --> 00:24:40,920
His yoke is easy.

378
00:24:40,920 --> 00:24:42,040
His burden is light.

379
00:24:42,040 --> 00:24:46,320
He has come that we might have life and life more abundantly.

380
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:51,460
But here's the thing, that life, and we're going to see this pictured in baptism, that life

381
00:24:51,460 --> 00:24:54,880
comes on the other side of self-denial and death.

382
00:24:54,880 --> 00:24:59,800
The whole point of the gospel is that life comes on the other side of death.

383
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:04,840
And so when we baptize people into the water, we're picturing that their old self, their

384
00:25:04,840 --> 00:25:09,500
self that was walking the wide road that leads to destruction, they're voluntarily dying to

385
00:25:09,500 --> 00:25:10,100
that person.

386
00:25:10,100 --> 00:25:14,740
And they are turning around 180 degrees and they are going down the narrow road that leads

387
00:25:14,740 --> 00:25:15,680
to life.

388
00:25:18,980 --> 00:25:24,440
And here's the thing, here's the thing about Saul is I think, I think by this point in

389
00:25:24,440 --> 00:25:29,580
Saul's life, he was having some internal confliction about the direction of his life.

390
00:25:29,580 --> 00:25:32,740
And this is how God works in your life and in my life, right?

391
00:25:32,740 --> 00:25:37,360
There's, as we're going down our road that we think is leading to life, we'll have these

392
00:25:37,360 --> 00:25:39,140
interactions with people.

393
00:25:39,520 --> 00:25:43,320
We'll have these signposts along the way of our life and we'll get these internal like,

394
00:25:43,320 --> 00:25:46,540
hmm, maybe this isn't working the way that I thought it was working.

395
00:25:46,540 --> 00:25:49,680
Maybe I'm not as happy as I thought I was.

396
00:25:49,680 --> 00:25:51,880
Maybe I'm not as confident as I thought I was.

397
00:25:51,880 --> 00:25:57,460
And I think, I think Saul was having these internal challenges in his life.

398
00:25:57,480 --> 00:26:03,760
And there's a couple of reasons I think that, um, the first reason is later in Acts, Saul

399
00:26:03,760 --> 00:26:06,880
recounts his interaction with God on the roads of Damascus.

400
00:26:06,880 --> 00:26:08,760
And we don't get it in Acts chapter nine.

401
00:26:08,760 --> 00:26:09,540
We'll get there in a minute.

402
00:26:09,540 --> 00:26:15,580
But when Saul recounts it, he said that, that Jesus said to him, is it hard for you to kick

403
00:26:15,580 --> 00:26:16,880
against the goads?

404
00:26:16,880 --> 00:26:22,360
There was this, there was this stabbing, this pricking that the Holy Spirit that God was

405
00:26:22,360 --> 00:26:25,760
doing to Saul and Saul knew internally, he was struggling.

406
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:28,040
He was like, man, I think I'm doing the right thing.

407
00:26:28,040 --> 00:26:33,560
But he was being poked and prodded like an animal who was going in the wrong direction.

408
00:26:33,560 --> 00:26:36,200
And Jesus was trying to say, Saul, you're going in the wrong direction.

409
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:39,900
You know, the Scriptures, you know, the Old Testament, wake up, you're going the wrong

410
00:26:39,900 --> 00:26:40,400
direction.

411
00:26:40,400 --> 00:26:42,840
Saul was having these internal conflicts.

412
00:26:42,840 --> 00:26:52,040
And yet he kept proudly pushing forward down his way that ultimately would lead to destruction.

413
00:26:52,360 --> 00:26:57,520
The second reason I think that is because he's asking for approval from spiritual leaders

414
00:26:57,520 --> 00:26:58,120
in his life.

415
00:26:58,120 --> 00:27:03,000
This is important because I think we do this all the time.

416
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:04,800
He's, he's confident.

417
00:27:04,800 --> 00:27:06,480
He's on his way to persecute the church.

418
00:27:06,480 --> 00:27:09,140
But I think there's this internal struggle that he's having.

419
00:27:09,140 --> 00:27:13,100
And so he's going to authorities that he looks up to, spiritual people that have influence

420
00:27:13,100 --> 00:27:13,680
in his life.

421
00:27:13,680 --> 00:27:15,380
And he's saying, I'm doing the right thing, right?

422
00:27:15,380 --> 00:27:17,220
Can you guys affirm me?

423
00:27:17,220 --> 00:27:21,920
Can you give me the documentation that I need so that when anybody asks, so that when I go

424
00:27:21,920 --> 00:27:24,240
to sleep at night, I can say, but they told me it was good.

425
00:27:24,240 --> 00:27:26,380
They told me it was right.

426
00:27:26,380 --> 00:27:31,940
And I think for those of us that are having these internal struggles with God, I think

427
00:27:31,940 --> 00:27:32,520
we do this.

428
00:27:32,520 --> 00:27:37,220
I think we look for people in authority to tell us the thing that we want to do.

429
00:27:37,220 --> 00:27:43,440
We go and search out and we find voices of people that are going to affirm our direction,

430
00:27:43,440 --> 00:27:45,240
whether or not it's God's direction or not.

431
00:27:46,320 --> 00:27:52,740
And I want to caution us that just because a person in authority gives you affirmation

432
00:27:52,740 --> 00:27:56,620
for your lifestyle does not mean that that is on behalf of God.

433
00:27:57,860 --> 00:28:01,680
And so if you are being convicted, challenged by the Holy Spirit, and you're like, you know

434
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:01,900
what?

435
00:28:01,900 --> 00:28:03,220
This person says it's good.

436
00:28:03,220 --> 00:28:04,260
This person says it's good.

437
00:28:04,260 --> 00:28:08,340
This group of people affirms my identity or my direction for my life.

438
00:28:08,340 --> 00:28:11,560
Just you do the work.

439
00:28:11,560 --> 00:28:12,220
You pause.

440
00:28:12,220 --> 00:28:16,180
You go back and you see, is this from God or is this from someone else?

441
00:28:16,980 --> 00:28:22,820
I had a really good friend a while back who confessed to me some pretty, pretty bad things

442
00:28:22,820 --> 00:28:24,080
that he was participating in.

443
00:28:24,080 --> 00:28:31,540
And I was super thankful that that confession happened and I gave him what I thought God

444
00:28:31,540 --> 00:28:34,020
would want him to do, how God would want him to respond.

445
00:28:34,020 --> 00:28:42,360
And though he had the bravery, the courage to confess, he didn't like the thing that I told

446
00:28:42,360 --> 00:28:43,540
him I thought God would want him to do.

447
00:28:45,080 --> 00:28:49,740
And he disagreed with me and so I got a couple of his friends that also loved him that cared

448
00:28:49,740 --> 00:28:52,120
about him and I said, we all think that this is the thing that you should do.

449
00:28:52,120 --> 00:29:01,060
And instead he went and he found people that were less in the know with the information and

450
00:29:01,060 --> 00:29:02,840
they affirmed the thing that he wanted to do anyway.

451
00:29:02,840 --> 00:29:11,600
And ultimately those people that were less familiar with the situation, they affirmed him

452
00:29:11,600 --> 00:29:13,520
to do a thing that I think does not honor God.

453
00:29:15,080 --> 00:29:17,080
And I share that story to share with you.

454
00:29:17,080 --> 00:29:21,700
I think we do this when we're convicted, when we're challenged, when we know what God wants

455
00:29:21,700 --> 00:29:26,520
us to do and we don't want to do it rather than humbling ourselves before God and doing

456
00:29:26,520 --> 00:29:28,820
the hard thing, the narrow roadway.

457
00:29:28,820 --> 00:29:33,980
We go and we find people that'll just tell us to keep doing the thing that we want to do.

458
00:29:35,620 --> 00:29:40,980
And those people are affirming us in our direction towards destruction.

459
00:29:40,980 --> 00:29:48,180
So Saul is on his way to do the thing that he thinks is right, looking for affirmation from

460
00:29:48,180 --> 00:29:51,440
other people so that he doesn't have to deal with this conviction that he has from God,

461
00:29:51,440 --> 00:29:53,460
this kicking against the goads.

462
00:29:53,460 --> 00:29:59,180
He hears from God that it's not what he should do and yet he continues to push forward in stubbornness.

463
00:29:59,180 --> 00:30:00,560
Remember we talked about this last week?

464
00:30:00,600 --> 00:30:05,360
He was stubborn, he was self-righteous, he keeps doing the thing he knows he shouldn't

465
00:30:05,360 --> 00:30:05,680
do.

466
00:30:05,680 --> 00:30:10,260
And because God loves Saul and has a plan for Saul, God says, I'm not going to let you go

467
00:30:10,260 --> 00:30:11,060
any further.

468
00:30:11,060 --> 00:30:17,360
Verse four, falling, suddenly a light from heaven shone around him and falling to the ground,

469
00:30:17,360 --> 00:30:21,480
he heard a voice saying to him, Saul, Saul, why are you persecuting me?

470
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:26,040
Saul said, who are you, Lord?

471
00:30:26,040 --> 00:30:32,540
And the voice replied, I am Jesus whom you are persecuting.

472
00:30:32,540 --> 00:30:38,360
But rise and enter the city and you will be told what you are to do.

473
00:30:38,360 --> 00:30:42,640
The men who were traveling with him stood speechless, hearing the voice but seeing no one.

474
00:30:42,640 --> 00:30:47,060
Saul rose from the ground and although his eyes were open, he saw nothing.

475
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:51,860
So they led him by the hand and brought him into Damascus and for three days he was without

476
00:30:51,860 --> 00:30:54,980
sight and he neither ate nor drank.

477
00:30:54,980 --> 00:30:58,920
God loves Saul.

478
00:30:58,920 --> 00:31:04,040
God has a plan for Saul and he lovingly confronts Saul in the midst of his rebellion.

479
00:31:04,040 --> 00:31:08,780
I think throughout the path, including Stephen's sermon, God was trying to get a hold of Saul's

480
00:31:08,780 --> 00:31:09,160
attention.

481
00:31:09,160 --> 00:31:11,700
He's trying to say, you're going in the opposite direction.

482
00:31:12,160 --> 00:31:14,740
You're going up, you're going the wrong way.

483
00:31:14,740 --> 00:31:16,900
Wake up, wake up, wake up.

484
00:31:16,900 --> 00:31:19,320
Saul continues to be self-righteous and stubborn.

485
00:31:19,320 --> 00:31:23,860
He keeps finding ways to convince himself that he's doing the right thing, that he is the

486
00:31:23,860 --> 00:31:24,980
hero of the story.

487
00:31:24,980 --> 00:31:26,920
And the whole time God is trying to get his attention.

488
00:31:26,920 --> 00:31:29,860
And finally, God said, enough is enough.

489
00:31:29,860 --> 00:31:33,680
And isn't this similar to a lot of our stories?

490
00:31:33,680 --> 00:31:36,780
Those of us that have been in the waters of baptism.

491
00:31:38,100 --> 00:31:43,000
Haven't we rebelled for a while, felt conviction and kept going?

492
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:47,900
And for some of us, it takes like a light from heaven, takes God smacking us in the back

493
00:31:47,900 --> 00:31:50,420
of the head and saying, enough is enough.

494
00:31:50,420 --> 00:31:52,460
You're going the wrong way.

495
00:31:52,460 --> 00:31:57,700
I love you too much to let you keep going in the opposite direction that I've called you

496
00:31:57,700 --> 00:31:57,920
to.

497
00:31:57,920 --> 00:32:04,100
So Jesus confronts Saul.

498
00:32:04,100 --> 00:32:05,400
He says, you're going in the wrong way.

499
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:08,020
He says, why are you persecuting me?

500
00:32:08,740 --> 00:32:09,660
I love this.

501
00:32:09,660 --> 00:32:13,580
Was Saul persecuting Jesus literally, physically?

502
00:32:13,580 --> 00:32:16,220
No, he's persecuting the church.

503
00:32:16,220 --> 00:32:18,660
He's persecuting the followers of Christ.

504
00:32:18,660 --> 00:32:23,540
But I think what's so important for us to learn about this is there's a spiritual reality

505
00:32:23,540 --> 00:32:26,680
at play here that Jesus, he loves his church so much.

506
00:32:26,680 --> 00:32:32,940
He is so ever present with his followers, those of us who follow the way that to persecute

507
00:32:32,940 --> 00:32:35,540
us is ultimately to persecute him.

508
00:32:36,200 --> 00:32:41,980
I think that it's true of the church, but I also think that that's true of all humanity.

509
00:32:41,980 --> 00:32:44,820
I think God created each and every single one of you.

510
00:32:44,820 --> 00:32:45,820
He loves you.

511
00:32:45,820 --> 00:32:50,960
And when you are wronged, when you are sinned against, when you are hurt, I think God kind

512
00:32:50,960 --> 00:32:57,800
of receives that as a sin against himself because he created you and someone sinned against you.

513
00:32:57,800 --> 00:33:04,360
And for God, God sits there with you and he receives the hurt that you received as his

514
00:33:04,360 --> 00:33:04,840
own hurt.

515
00:33:04,900 --> 00:33:10,060
And for those of us who have been deeply wounded by others, I think this should comfort you.

516
00:33:10,060 --> 00:33:17,560
That it was not God's plan that you were hurt, that you were sinned against, that you were

517
00:33:17,560 --> 00:33:19,040
taken advantage of or abused.

518
00:33:19,040 --> 00:33:21,420
That was not God's plan and God does not affirm that.

519
00:33:21,420 --> 00:33:26,640
As a matter of fact, God loves you so much that he views that offense as an offense against

520
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:27,440
himself.

521
00:33:27,440 --> 00:33:38,380
This is God's response to those of us who are walking our own way.

522
00:33:40,020 --> 00:33:42,580
My belief is God will ultimately confront you.

523
00:33:42,580 --> 00:33:48,280
My belief is God probably is confronting you along the way that he's putting up signs on

524
00:33:48,280 --> 00:33:50,420
your road, down your own way to get your attention.

525
00:33:50,420 --> 00:33:55,400
That this life ultimately, as fun as it might be, as enjoyable as it might be, it will not

526
00:33:55,400 --> 00:33:57,680
lead to your flourishing.

527
00:33:57,680 --> 00:34:01,280
Saul, or God grabs Saul's attention.

528
00:34:01,280 --> 00:34:09,480
He's always lovingly confronting us and providing us with opportunities to repent.

529
00:34:10,020 --> 00:34:13,580
And that language, it's important that we understand that language of repentance.

530
00:34:13,580 --> 00:34:17,140
We've talked about it in the past, so I won't belabor it, but repentance literally just means

531
00:34:17,140 --> 00:34:20,980
to stop and to turn around and go in the opposite direction.

532
00:34:20,980 --> 00:34:24,920
Doesn't that line up with the spiritual ways that we're talking about?

533
00:34:24,920 --> 00:34:26,900
There's really only two ways that we can be walking.

534
00:34:26,900 --> 00:34:31,660
And repentance is we're walking our own way down the wide road that leads to destruction.

535
00:34:31,660 --> 00:34:35,680
And God is trying to get our attention to let us see that there's a ledge there that

536
00:34:35,680 --> 00:34:36,620
we're about to walk off.

537
00:34:36,620 --> 00:34:39,980
Not because he's a cosmic tyrant, but because he's a loving father and he says,

538
00:34:40,020 --> 00:34:46,580
you're about to walk off the side of the cliff, please stop, repent, turn around and go my

539
00:34:46,580 --> 00:34:46,840
way.

540
00:34:46,840 --> 00:34:50,820
Go the way that leads to life and life more abundantly.

541
00:34:50,820 --> 00:34:52,880
This is the invitation of the gospel.

542
00:34:52,880 --> 00:34:57,640
And God is lovingly confronting all of his people.

543
00:34:57,640 --> 00:35:01,160
There's two of my favorite verses that point this out because we don't always see it.

544
00:35:02,160 --> 00:35:06,280
Ecclesiastes 3.11 says that God has placed eternity in your heart.

545
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:13,440
It means somehow in some spiritual way, you know what you were created for.

546
00:35:13,440 --> 00:35:17,720
You know that you were created for a relationship with the father, the creator of the universe.

547
00:35:17,720 --> 00:35:23,000
You know that there is an order in creation by which you are to participate in this whole

548
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:24,080
cosmic kingdom.

549
00:35:25,340 --> 00:35:29,220
And when you go in the opposite direction, there is internal conflict.

550
00:35:29,220 --> 00:35:31,100
Not always.

551
00:35:31,100 --> 00:35:37,080
And we numb it and we push it to the side and we get other people to affirm our belief system

552
00:35:37,080 --> 00:35:39,120
so that we can ignore the conviction that's happening.

553
00:35:39,120 --> 00:35:45,400
But ultimately, all of us, I believe God is confronting with the spiritual reality of eternity.

554
00:35:45,400 --> 00:35:51,180
He's trying to get us to understand that we're living for things less than what he has for us.

555
00:35:51,680 --> 00:35:53,900
Second verse is Romans 1, verses 19 and 20.

556
00:35:53,900 --> 00:35:58,860
It says that God has clearly revealed himself to the world through his creative order.

557
00:35:58,860 --> 00:36:05,160
Again, just the way that God created and made things, it's supposed to awaken our eyes to the fact

558
00:36:05,160 --> 00:36:06,180
that he's a loving father.

559
00:36:06,180 --> 00:36:12,340
And oftentimes we put that to the side.

560
00:36:12,340 --> 00:36:17,400
Jesus said to Saul, is it hard for you to kick against the goad?

561
00:36:18,320 --> 00:36:22,660
God was providing signposts along the way for Saul to realize he was going in the wrong direction.

562
00:36:22,660 --> 00:36:27,440
And Saul continually ignored them until finally God made it too obvious for him to ignore.

563
00:36:27,440 --> 00:36:40,800
So I think ultimately all of us, if we walk down the wide road that leads to destruction long enough,

564
00:36:40,800 --> 00:36:44,000
we will have our own Damascus Road experience.

565
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:48,600
It might not be a light from heaven and Jesus speaking audibly or directly to us,

566
00:36:48,600 --> 00:36:50,320
but oftentimes it is rock bottom.

567
00:36:50,320 --> 00:36:56,900
Like we take this road as far as it will allow us to go, and we hit this rock bottom.

568
00:36:56,900 --> 00:37:03,380
And it's in that rock bottom that God often meets us on the ground, blind, humble, and says,

569
00:37:03,380 --> 00:37:04,620
there's a better way.

570
00:37:04,620 --> 00:37:06,780
There's a better way.

571
00:37:09,080 --> 00:37:10,880
I love what Alan Bandy says.

572
00:37:10,880 --> 00:37:11,240
He says,

573
00:37:11,240 --> 00:37:16,840
to ascend to God, one must often first descend into darkness and defeat.

574
00:37:16,840 --> 00:37:19,640
It often takes us hitting that rock bottom.

575
00:37:19,640 --> 00:37:26,100
It often takes us realizing, being humbled, that our way isn't working the way that we would let others to believe that it is.

576
00:37:26,100 --> 00:37:28,820
And this is where Saul was.

577
00:37:28,820 --> 00:37:32,120
Saul was acting with bravado, with pride, with confidence.

578
00:37:32,440 --> 00:37:37,380
He was trying to let everyone around him know that he was confident, that he was going the way that he was supposed to be going.

579
00:37:37,380 --> 00:37:44,240
But internally, there was a struggle, there was a wrestle, and eventually God brought him to his rock bottom.

580
00:37:44,240 --> 00:37:50,060
To those of you in the room that are still walking that road, I would just invite you, do not wait.

581
00:37:50,060 --> 00:37:53,820
Do not wait until your life hits rock bottom.

582
00:37:53,820 --> 00:37:59,020
Do not wait until the road that you're taking leads you to a dead end.

583
00:37:59,580 --> 00:38:02,340
Today, if you hear the voice of the Lord, do not harden your heart.

584
00:38:02,340 --> 00:38:08,520
So, two spiritual ways.

585
00:38:08,520 --> 00:38:11,500
If you're going the opposite way, God will ultimately confront you.

586
00:38:11,500 --> 00:38:13,760
He probably already has begun that process.

587
00:38:13,760 --> 00:38:22,620
He brings Saul to his knees from a proud man, acting with confidence, to a humble man, blind.

588
00:38:22,620 --> 00:38:24,760
And then he changes the scene.

589
00:38:24,760 --> 00:38:26,620
I love that Luke changes the scene here.

590
00:38:26,620 --> 00:38:29,200
He invites another person into the room.

591
00:38:29,500 --> 00:38:31,620
So, Saul gets to Damascus blind.

592
00:38:31,620 --> 00:38:34,020
He doesn't eat for three days.

593
00:38:34,020 --> 00:38:35,700
Verse 10.

594
00:38:35,700 --> 00:38:39,400
Now, there was a disciple at Damascus named Ananias.

595
00:38:39,400 --> 00:38:41,780
I love the juxtaposition here.

596
00:38:41,780 --> 00:38:49,960
There was Saul walking his way in disobedience, and now waiting for him in Damascus is a follower of the way, listening for obedience.

597
00:38:50,900 --> 00:38:55,640
Now, there was a disciple at Damascus named Ananias, and the Lord said to him in a vision, Ananias.

598
00:38:57,480 --> 00:38:58,900
Ananias responded, here I am, Lord.

599
00:38:58,900 --> 00:39:04,740
And the Lord said to him, rise and go to a street called Straight, and at the house of Judas, look for a man of Tarsus named Saul.

600
00:39:04,740 --> 00:39:06,100
For behold, he is praying.

601
00:39:06,100 --> 00:39:09,140
He has seen a vision of a man named Ananias.

602
00:39:09,140 --> 00:39:12,580
Come in and lay his hands on him so that he might regain his sight.

603
00:39:13,880 --> 00:39:19,540
But Ananias answered, Lord, I have heard from many about this man, how much evil he has done to your saints at Jerusalem,

604
00:39:19,540 --> 00:39:24,820
and that he has authority from the chief priests to bind all who call on your name.

605
00:39:25,540 --> 00:39:33,800
But the Lord said to him, go, for he is a chosen instrument of mine to carry my name before the Gentiles and the kings and the children of Israel,

606
00:39:33,800 --> 00:39:37,960
for I will show him how much he must suffer for my namesake.

607
00:39:37,960 --> 00:39:45,420
So Ananias departed, and he entered the house, and laying hands on him, he said,

608
00:39:45,420 --> 00:39:54,860
Brother Saul, the Lord Jesus who appeared to you on the road by which you came has sent me so that you may regain your sight and be filled with the Holy Spirit.

609
00:39:55,540 --> 00:40:02,940
It's the part in the story where we see God using the participation, the obedience of others,

610
00:40:02,940 --> 00:40:06,360
and the way in which he wants to interact with our lives.

611
00:40:06,360 --> 00:40:13,060
He wants us to participate in his plan of taking people from going in their own way and redirecting them,

612
00:40:13,060 --> 00:40:15,980
having them repent and go in the way that he has called them to.

613
00:40:15,980 --> 00:40:18,900
He wants our participation in that.

614
00:40:18,900 --> 00:40:25,240
God tells Ananias, I have a purpose for you, and that purpose is going to involve Saul's repentance.

615
00:40:25,500 --> 00:40:29,960
And I think rightly so, Ananias has a few questions, right?

616
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:37,420
He's like, yeah, we've been praying that when that guy gets here that something will happen so that he can't kill us,

617
00:40:37,420 --> 00:40:39,300
and now you're telling me that he's blind?

618
00:40:39,300 --> 00:40:41,160
That sounds like an answered prayer to me.

619
00:40:41,160 --> 00:40:45,540
God's like, yeah, I appreciate your prayers.

620
00:40:45,540 --> 00:40:49,080
I heard them, and actually my plan is better than the plan that you think it is.

621
00:40:49,080 --> 00:40:52,820
So you think I'm going to blind him and stop him from persecuting you,

622
00:40:52,900 --> 00:40:54,760
but actually I'm going to get a hold of his attention.

623
00:40:54,760 --> 00:40:57,340
I'm going to flip his life 180 degrees around.

624
00:40:57,340 --> 00:41:00,840
I'm going to use you to extend my grace and my forgiveness to him.

625
00:41:00,840 --> 00:41:05,760
He's going to understand the gospel, and he is going to go and preach the gospel to the kings

626
00:41:05,760 --> 00:41:08,320
and to the Gentiles and to the house of Israel.

627
00:41:09,480 --> 00:41:15,220
God's plan is so much better than our plan, and he's calling us to participate in it.

628
00:41:15,220 --> 00:41:22,440
And it's okay if we have some questions, but at the end of the day, what he ultimately wants from us is our obedience.

629
00:41:24,800 --> 00:41:27,620
Isn't this a beautiful picture of the kingdom of God?

630
00:41:27,620 --> 00:41:32,500
He regularly uses our obedience to impact the lives of those around us.

631
00:41:32,500 --> 00:41:34,340
And here's the thing.

632
00:41:34,340 --> 00:41:36,700
God doesn't need Ananias' obedience.

633
00:41:36,700 --> 00:41:38,280
Right?

634
00:41:38,280 --> 00:41:43,160
Like God showed up at the road to Damascus, blinded him, and talked to him.

635
00:41:44,000 --> 00:41:48,860
God's got all the tools he needs to make Saul turn around and walk in the opposite direction.

636
00:41:48,860 --> 00:41:51,860
But he invites Ananias here, and I think it's beautiful.

637
00:41:51,860 --> 00:41:57,280
It's so beautiful because God often is doing so much more than we could ever get our minds around.

638
00:41:57,840 --> 00:42:03,700
Because by inviting Ananias to obedience, he's doing something both in Saul's life and Ananias' life.

639
00:42:03,700 --> 00:42:10,820
By using Ananias, he was able to do a healing work in Saul's life,

640
00:42:10,820 --> 00:42:16,480
and he was able to teach Ananias a very important lesson about the grace and forgiveness of God.

641
00:42:16,480 --> 00:42:25,440
I'm trying to decide what I want to do here.

642
00:42:27,840 --> 00:42:30,820
All right, we're just going to go fast, because I don't want to skip anything,

643
00:42:30,820 --> 00:42:32,580
just in case the Lord wanted you to hear it.

644
00:42:32,580 --> 00:42:35,240
So, I want to emphasize two points here.

645
00:42:35,240 --> 00:42:39,700
The first is that God will intentionally use you to have an impact in the lives of those around you.

646
00:42:39,700 --> 00:42:42,100
He will.

647
00:42:42,100 --> 00:42:46,860
He has a plan to use your life to influence the lives of others.

648
00:42:46,860 --> 00:42:49,480
Do you believe that?

649
00:42:49,480 --> 00:42:51,540
And are you looking for opportunities?

650
00:42:51,540 --> 00:42:54,940
Are you listening for opportunities for God to call you to obedience?

651
00:42:56,860 --> 00:42:59,020
It's one of the things I love about how we do baptism here.

652
00:42:59,020 --> 00:43:00,760
When we have people that sign up to do baptism,

653
00:43:00,760 --> 00:43:03,980
the first question I ask them after we make sure they understand the gospel

654
00:43:03,980 --> 00:43:06,240
and what they're signing up for is I say,

655
00:43:06,240 --> 00:43:08,720
who's been spiritually influential in your life?

656
00:43:08,720 --> 00:43:10,540
Would you want them to baptize you?

657
00:43:10,540 --> 00:43:14,660
So, oftentimes the people that are doing the baptism

658
00:43:14,660 --> 00:43:18,500
are the people that God has used in influencing these people towards Jesus.

659
00:43:18,500 --> 00:43:22,020
It's a visible representation of how God works in the kingdom.

660
00:43:22,140 --> 00:43:24,300
It's not the pastor that does all the spiritual work.

661
00:43:24,300 --> 00:43:25,680
It's you.

662
00:43:25,680 --> 00:43:26,160
It's me.

663
00:43:26,160 --> 00:43:27,220
It's in our neighborhood.

664
00:43:27,220 --> 00:43:28,860
It's in our workplace.

665
00:43:28,860 --> 00:43:31,460
We are the ones doing the kingdom work.

666
00:43:31,460 --> 00:43:35,080
God often uses us in the lives of others.

667
00:43:36,780 --> 00:43:40,440
And what I would love, what I would love more than anything in our church

668
00:43:40,440 --> 00:43:42,060
is I would love for it to become a competition

669
00:43:42,060 --> 00:43:45,240
of who gets to baptize the most people, right?

670
00:43:45,240 --> 00:43:47,740
I would love for us to get to a place

671
00:43:47,740 --> 00:43:51,220
where we're looking for God to use us so much so that we're like,

672
00:43:51,220 --> 00:43:53,860
man, next time there's a baptism, I need to be up there.

673
00:43:53,860 --> 00:43:56,020
And look, at the end of the day, the work is on God.

674
00:43:56,020 --> 00:43:57,260
Like, God has to do the work.

675
00:43:57,260 --> 00:43:59,820
But man, if we would posture ourselves in a way

676
00:43:59,820 --> 00:44:02,300
where we're constantly looking to be obedient

677
00:44:02,300 --> 00:44:03,860
and used in the life of others,

678
00:44:03,860 --> 00:44:05,300
how incredible would that be?

679
00:44:05,300 --> 00:44:08,140
And how much more often would we have to fill this baptism tank?

680
00:44:08,140 --> 00:44:13,600
So no matter what message you've heard from others in your life

681
00:44:13,600 --> 00:44:15,080
or what you might think about yourself,

682
00:44:15,080 --> 00:44:17,540
I want you to know you have a role to play in God's kingdom.

683
00:44:17,540 --> 00:44:20,060
There are no bench players on Team Jesus.

684
00:44:21,760 --> 00:44:23,580
Are you expecting to be used by Him?

685
00:44:23,580 --> 00:44:25,620
Are you willing to be obedient to His invitation?

686
00:44:25,620 --> 00:44:27,080
The second thing I want to point out here

687
00:44:27,080 --> 00:44:29,160
is that the work God is...

688
00:44:29,160 --> 00:44:31,980
All right.

689
00:44:31,980 --> 00:44:34,900
The work that God is calling you to do

690
00:44:34,900 --> 00:44:38,280
might include the very person that you least want to engage with

691
00:44:38,280 --> 00:44:39,680
or extend grace to.

692
00:44:39,680 --> 00:44:45,140
Let's not brush past the fact that Saul likely had a hand

693
00:44:45,140 --> 00:44:48,180
in killing or imprisoning literal friends of Ananias.

694
00:44:48,180 --> 00:44:51,080
And God is saying, Ananias, I want you to go

695
00:44:51,080 --> 00:44:52,800
and I want you to place your hands on Him

696
00:44:52,800 --> 00:44:55,660
so that He might be healed and receive the Holy Spirit.

697
00:44:55,660 --> 00:44:59,900
And for the godliest people in the room,

698
00:44:59,900 --> 00:45:03,220
we might say, like, yeah, we want our enemies to receive forgiveness.

699
00:45:03,220 --> 00:45:05,760
But don't make me put my hands on them.

700
00:45:05,760 --> 00:45:07,360
Right?

701
00:45:07,360 --> 00:45:11,180
Don't make me touch that guy or that girl that did that thing to me.

702
00:45:11,180 --> 00:45:14,620
This is the heart of the gospel,

703
00:45:14,620 --> 00:45:17,320
that Jesus loved us and He gave His life for us

704
00:45:17,320 --> 00:45:19,540
when we were His enemies.

705
00:45:20,400 --> 00:45:24,420
And His call to those of us who have decided to turn from the wide road

706
00:45:24,420 --> 00:45:25,300
that leads to destruction

707
00:45:25,300 --> 00:45:27,160
and head the narrow road that leads to life,

708
00:45:27,160 --> 00:45:31,280
His call for us is that we would love our enemies the way that He loved us.

709
00:45:31,280 --> 00:45:34,620
So who is it in your life that you've written off?

710
00:45:34,620 --> 00:45:38,020
Who is it that you think is too far gone?

711
00:45:38,020 --> 00:45:41,560
Who is it that you assume will not listen to you?

712
00:45:43,740 --> 00:45:49,160
Who might God be calling you to share the message of hope with or minister to?

713
00:45:50,540 --> 00:45:54,080
Who might God be calling you to lay your hands on and heal through the power of forgiveness?

714
00:45:54,080 --> 00:45:57,020
See, I know far too many Christians.

715
00:45:57,020 --> 00:46:02,900
And I speak from a place of privilege because I've been wounded deeply,

716
00:46:02,900 --> 00:46:05,800
but not to the level that some of you have been.

717
00:46:07,040 --> 00:46:10,280
But at the end of the day, I see far too many Christians who hold on to bitterness

718
00:46:10,280 --> 00:46:12,500
and unforgiveness towards others for far too long.

719
00:46:12,500 --> 00:46:18,300
And not only are you keeping them from an opportunity to hear, to receive,

720
00:46:18,300 --> 00:46:20,460
to experience the gospel of Jesus,

721
00:46:20,460 --> 00:46:23,640
but you're holding on to bitterness that God does not want you to hold on to.

722
00:46:23,640 --> 00:46:27,080
It's actually leading you to rot and decay in your soul.

723
00:46:29,660 --> 00:46:34,000
So who might God be calling you to to go to lay your hands on to and say,

724
00:46:34,000 --> 00:46:37,440
I forgive you because Jesus forgave me.

725
00:46:37,440 --> 00:46:39,340
And I don't excuse what you did to me.

726
00:46:39,340 --> 00:46:42,320
And I'm not going to put myself in a position where you can do it to me again,

727
00:46:42,320 --> 00:46:43,080
but I forgive you.

728
00:46:43,080 --> 00:46:50,900
I will skip this because we already talked about it a little bit.

729
00:46:50,900 --> 00:46:55,460
But the reason we spent so much time on Saul's life and background last week

730
00:46:55,460 --> 00:46:56,520
is for this point here.

731
00:46:58,200 --> 00:47:02,260
Verse 16, 15.

732
00:47:02,260 --> 00:47:04,780
Saul tells Ananias to go,

733
00:47:04,780 --> 00:47:08,080
for he is a chosen instrument of mine to carry my name before the Gentiles

734
00:47:08,080 --> 00:47:09,840
and the kings and the children of Israel.

735
00:47:09,840 --> 00:47:12,660
See, God orchestrated Saul's life.

736
00:47:12,660 --> 00:47:17,040
The experiences of Saul's life, where he was born, where he grew up,

737
00:47:17,040 --> 00:47:18,780
the things that he knew about the Old Testament,

738
00:47:18,780 --> 00:47:21,180
the things that he knew about Roman culture and philosophy,

739
00:47:21,180 --> 00:47:24,100
God had orchestrated all of those things.

740
00:47:24,100 --> 00:47:27,500
It made Saul the perfect candidate to be the apostle,

741
00:47:27,680 --> 00:47:31,040
to the Gentiles, and to the rest of Israel.

742
00:47:31,040 --> 00:47:36,160
He was the perfect person to bridge the gap between the nation of Israel and the Gentiles.

743
00:47:37,980 --> 00:47:43,240
And I believe, ultimately, in some way, shape, or form, the same is true for you and me.

744
00:47:43,240 --> 00:47:46,360
That God has created you on purpose and for a purpose.

745
00:47:46,360 --> 00:47:51,300
Ephesians 2 says that you are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus to do good works,

746
00:47:51,300 --> 00:47:53,300
which he prepared in advance for you to do.

747
00:47:53,300 --> 00:47:54,880
Not for me to do.

748
00:47:54,880 --> 00:47:59,320
There are works for you to do, that I cannot do, that no one else in this room can do.

749
00:47:59,420 --> 00:48:01,840
God has a purpose and a plan for you.

750
00:48:01,840 --> 00:48:03,500
Do you believe that?

751
00:48:03,500 --> 00:48:05,680
Do you believe that God knit you together in your mother's womb,

752
00:48:05,680 --> 00:48:08,420
that he gave you your personalities, your skills, and your passions,

753
00:48:08,420 --> 00:48:10,440
that he allowed you to have experiences that you had?

754
00:48:10,440 --> 00:48:13,760
Even the bad experiences, that he allowed those experiences

755
00:48:13,760 --> 00:48:18,060
so that you might have a ministry of reconciliation through your pain.

756
00:48:20,780 --> 00:48:23,900
All so that you can play a unique role in the kingdom of God.

757
00:48:23,900 --> 00:48:26,660
There are no second-class citizens in the kingdom of God.

758
00:48:26,660 --> 00:48:28,140
All of us are needed at the table.

759
00:48:28,140 --> 00:48:31,480
All right.

760
00:48:31,480 --> 00:48:33,320
Last.

761
00:48:33,320 --> 00:48:36,220
All of this crescendos to one thing.

762
00:48:36,220 --> 00:48:38,620
Saul being baptized.

763
00:48:38,620 --> 00:48:40,920
So Ananias departed.

764
00:48:40,920 --> 00:48:42,520
He entered the house, laying his hands on him.

765
00:48:42,520 --> 00:48:42,780
He said,

766
00:48:42,780 --> 00:48:46,460
Brother, brother, Saul, can you imagine that moment?

767
00:48:48,200 --> 00:48:53,200
Ananias, filled with anger and bitterness and frustration towards Saul

768
00:48:53,200 --> 00:48:55,280
and the pain that he caused, his friends and family,

769
00:48:55,280 --> 00:49:00,300
receiving enough, just enough, mustering up just enough grace of God

770
00:49:00,300 --> 00:49:01,380
to say, you know what?

771
00:49:01,380 --> 00:49:03,160
Welcome to the family.

772
00:49:03,160 --> 00:49:04,940
I forgive you.

773
00:49:04,940 --> 00:49:09,200
You imagine Saul, who had literally killed Christians up to this point,

774
00:49:09,200 --> 00:49:14,260
being touched by a follower of the way and saying,

775
00:49:14,260 --> 00:49:15,340
welcome to the family.

776
00:49:16,940 --> 00:49:19,780
This is the transforming power of the gospel.

777
00:49:19,780 --> 00:49:25,060
Brother Saul, the Lord Jesus, who appeared to you on the road by which you came,

778
00:49:25,060 --> 00:49:29,440
has sent me so that you may regain your sight and be filled with the Holy Spirit.

779
00:49:29,440 --> 00:49:32,460
And immediately something like scales froze from his eyes.

780
00:49:32,460 --> 00:49:33,320
He regained his sight.

781
00:49:33,320 --> 00:49:35,020
He arose and was baptized.

782
00:49:35,020 --> 00:49:41,560
Again, the crescendo of this incredible story is Saul's baptism,

783
00:49:41,560 --> 00:49:44,120
a symbol that he had received God's call on his life,

784
00:49:44,120 --> 00:49:47,160
that he had stopped walking down the wide road that leads to destruction.

785
00:49:47,160 --> 00:49:47,860
He had repented.

786
00:49:47,860 --> 00:49:53,060
He had turned and he had started walking down the narrow road that ultimately leads to life.

787
00:49:53,060 --> 00:49:54,340
And here's the thing.

788
00:49:54,340 --> 00:49:57,120
This story would become a monument for the early church

789
00:49:57,120 --> 00:49:59,000
and the church throughout human history,

790
00:49:59,000 --> 00:50:01,780
that no one is too far gone for the grace of God.

791
00:50:02,540 --> 00:50:04,780
I don't care where you've been, what you've done.

792
00:50:04,780 --> 00:50:06,260
I don't care what you were doing last night.

793
00:50:06,260 --> 00:50:09,460
There is no one who is too far gone for the grace of God.

794
00:50:09,460 --> 00:50:14,140
Saul would later write to Timothy.

795
00:50:14,140 --> 00:50:15,980
I love this.

796
00:50:17,380 --> 00:50:21,700
Here is a trustworthy saying that deserves full acceptance.

797
00:50:21,700 --> 00:50:26,860
Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners, of whom I am the worst.

798
00:50:26,860 --> 00:50:33,020
For that very reason, because I was the worst,

799
00:50:33,020 --> 00:50:39,480
God has shown his patience as an example, as a monument for all those who would believe in him

800
00:50:39,480 --> 00:50:40,860
and receive eternal life.

801
00:50:40,860 --> 00:50:45,440
Saul is saying, look, God showed up so visibly, so intentionally in my life,

802
00:50:45,440 --> 00:50:46,660
because I was a murderer.

803
00:50:46,660 --> 00:50:49,120
I was literally killing his people.

804
00:50:49,120 --> 00:50:54,240
He did that so that his people would realize there is no one too far gone for the grace of God.

805
00:50:54,240 --> 00:50:59,340
I am an example that God's grace extends to anyone.

806
00:50:59,340 --> 00:51:04,600
So maybe you're here, you've been running for a long time.

807
00:51:04,600 --> 00:51:08,960
You've convinced yourself you're too far gone.

808
00:51:08,960 --> 00:51:12,320
You've convinced yourself that your way is the right way

809
00:51:12,320 --> 00:51:14,820
and that this way is ultimately going to lead to your satisfaction

810
00:51:14,820 --> 00:51:15,680
and to your life.

811
00:51:15,680 --> 00:51:19,160
I'm here to tell you that God has been placing signposts along the way

812
00:51:19,160 --> 00:51:21,240
to tell you that there is a cliff up ahead

813
00:51:21,240 --> 00:51:23,180
and that you will hit rock bottom eventually.

814
00:51:23,180 --> 00:51:26,360
How will you respond?

815
00:51:26,360 --> 00:51:30,100
Will you receive that confrontation?

816
00:51:30,100 --> 00:51:32,520
Will you turn and will you repent?

817
00:51:32,520 --> 00:51:35,760
Maybe you're here and you've submitted your life to him.

818
00:51:35,760 --> 00:51:39,680
You've been repeatedly giving in to the same sin or temptation.

819
00:51:39,680 --> 00:51:44,900
Let the story of Saul be a reminder to you that even in the midst of your continual brokenness,

820
00:51:44,900 --> 00:51:49,060
continual disobedience, that there is continual grace.

821
00:51:49,060 --> 00:51:51,900
But like we read in Romans 6,

822
00:51:51,900 --> 00:51:54,960
that grace is not so that you can keep on sinning and sinning and sinning and sinning.

823
00:51:54,960 --> 00:51:58,540
That grace is so that you can realize that your sin is going to lead you to death

824
00:51:58,540 --> 00:52:00,540
and that you can walk in the opposite direction.

825
00:52:03,960 --> 00:52:04,860
Here's my main point.

826
00:52:04,860 --> 00:52:06,180
We're done.

827
00:52:06,180 --> 00:52:06,640
I promise.

828
00:52:06,640 --> 00:52:09,000
I worked really hard on this main point.

829
00:52:09,000 --> 00:52:11,140
It rhymes, kind of.

830
00:52:11,140 --> 00:52:15,460
So if you're taking notes, this is what I want you to remember from this whole morning.

831
00:52:15,460 --> 00:52:21,480
That God is in the business of redirecting people from their way to the way.

832
00:52:21,480 --> 00:52:25,060
And he often uses us as guides along the way.

833
00:52:25,060 --> 00:52:30,860
God, he is in the business of redirecting people from their way to the way.

834
00:52:30,960 --> 00:52:32,180
There are two spiritual directions.

835
00:52:32,180 --> 00:52:34,940
We're all either going the wide road that leads to destruction

836
00:52:34,940 --> 00:52:36,700
or the narrow road that leads to life.

837
00:52:36,700 --> 00:52:39,240
And God is constantly, as a loving father,

838
00:52:39,240 --> 00:52:42,220
trying to redirect people who are walking towards this cliff.

839
00:52:42,220 --> 00:52:45,900
He's trying to invite them to life and to life more abundantly.

840
00:52:45,900 --> 00:52:47,340
And here's what he does.

841
00:52:47,340 --> 00:52:49,460
He uses us along the way.

842
00:52:49,460 --> 00:52:53,480
Yes, he can shine down a light from heaven,

843
00:52:53,480 --> 00:52:57,280
but far more often than not, he uses you and me in the lives of others.

844
00:53:00,600 --> 00:53:04,880
So, if you're in here and you haven't yet decided to follow Jesus,

845
00:53:04,880 --> 00:53:07,600
maybe today is the day.

846
00:53:07,600 --> 00:53:11,280
Maybe there's been signposts along the way,

847
00:53:11,280 --> 00:53:12,920
there's been conviction, and you're just like,

848
00:53:12,920 --> 00:53:15,820
nah, I'm good, I'm going to keep doing my own thing.

849
00:53:15,820 --> 00:53:20,700
My prayer today is that you would realize that you've been walking down a road

850
00:53:20,700 --> 00:53:22,540
that ultimately will lead to your destruction,

851
00:53:22,540 --> 00:53:26,040
and that God is a loving father who's inviting you to repent

852
00:53:26,040 --> 00:53:27,760
and to turn and go the opposite direction,

853
00:53:27,760 --> 00:53:31,900
not because he's a cosmic tyrant that demands obedience

854
00:53:31,900 --> 00:53:35,700
because he's a loving father that wants you to experience life and life more abundantly.

855
00:53:35,700 --> 00:53:41,960
Continue down this path, and it will lead to destruction,

856
00:53:41,960 --> 00:53:44,740
but repent and follow his way, and it will lead to life.

857
00:53:47,040 --> 00:53:51,740
Followers of Jesus, are you expecting God to use you to have an impact in the lives of others?

858
00:53:51,740 --> 00:53:56,560
Do you view yourself as a guide along the path of others' lives?

859
00:53:56,560 --> 00:54:01,080
And who might God be calling you to minister to or to bring hope and healing,

860
00:54:01,080 --> 00:54:03,240
the hope and healing of the presence of Jesus?

861
00:54:03,240 --> 00:54:07,940
Don't underestimate what God wants to do in your life.

862
00:54:08,500 --> 00:54:09,800
All right, so we're going to end with baptism.

863
00:54:09,800 --> 00:54:11,420
We try to make some space.

864
00:54:11,420 --> 00:54:13,300
Our kids are going to come in here in just a second

865
00:54:13,300 --> 00:54:16,300
because we want our kids to be in here and to see baptism

866
00:54:16,300 --> 00:54:18,120
and to celebrate baptism with us

867
00:54:18,120 --> 00:54:21,860
because it is the crescendo of the Christian life, right?

868
00:54:21,860 --> 00:54:24,800
It is like this is the turning point of going your own way

869
00:54:24,800 --> 00:54:27,120
and turning and repenting and going the way of Jesus.

870
00:54:27,120 --> 00:54:30,280
Baptism is the perfect way to end this message

871
00:54:30,280 --> 00:54:33,620
because it's exactly how Saul's story ends

872
00:54:33,620 --> 00:54:36,460
and God's story through Saul begins.

873
00:54:36,460 --> 00:54:39,000
This is baptism.

874
00:54:39,000 --> 00:54:40,520
Saul's story ends

875
00:54:40,520 --> 00:54:43,680
and God's story through Saul begins.

876
00:54:43,680 --> 00:54:47,960
We're saying I have died to my old self

877
00:54:47,960 --> 00:54:50,780
that was walking the wide road

878
00:54:50,780 --> 00:54:53,700
and I have been born again, made new.

879
00:54:53,700 --> 00:54:56,300
I'm a new person going a new direction.

880
00:54:56,300 --> 00:54:57,340
And will you be perfect?

881
00:54:57,340 --> 00:54:58,920
Absolutely not.

882
00:54:58,920 --> 00:55:02,320
Will you find yourself again and again

883
00:55:02,320 --> 00:55:04,660
feeling the pull of culture

884
00:55:04,660 --> 00:55:06,120
and the pressure of your friends

885
00:55:06,120 --> 00:55:08,560
to turn and go back the opposite direction?

886
00:55:08,560 --> 00:55:09,020
Yes.

887
00:55:09,020 --> 00:55:10,200
Will you have muscle memory?

888
00:55:10,200 --> 00:55:12,980
Will you step out of your house from time to time

889
00:55:12,980 --> 00:55:14,680
and start back down that wide road

890
00:55:14,680 --> 00:55:16,800
and it take a while for you to realize like,

891
00:55:16,800 --> 00:55:20,180
oh wait, we're not going that way anymore.

892
00:55:20,180 --> 00:55:21,900
You ever moved?

893
00:55:21,900 --> 00:55:23,600
You ever lived in a town

894
00:55:23,600 --> 00:55:26,260
and moved from that like in the same town?

895
00:55:26,260 --> 00:55:29,700
But like the path you go out of your house

896
00:55:29,700 --> 00:55:32,040
is different from how you normally do?

897
00:55:32,040 --> 00:55:33,240
Anybody else have that experience?

898
00:55:33,240 --> 00:55:36,240
It's awful because like for three weeks

899
00:55:36,240 --> 00:55:36,920
you get in your car

900
00:55:36,920 --> 00:55:38,860
and you just go back towards your old house

901
00:55:38,860 --> 00:55:40,880
and you're like, oh wait,

902
00:55:40,880 --> 00:55:42,120
this isn't where I live anymore.

903
00:55:42,120 --> 00:55:46,360
So that is often going to be your experience.

904
00:55:46,360 --> 00:55:47,940
As you repent, as you turn to Jesus,

905
00:55:47,940 --> 00:55:49,280
you will walk out of your house

906
00:55:49,280 --> 00:55:50,840
and start going the opposite direction.

907
00:55:50,840 --> 00:55:53,880
You will continue in patterns of sin,

908
00:55:53,880 --> 00:55:56,820
but the Holy Spirit has power to give you victory.

909
00:56:01,380 --> 00:56:03,520
Baptism is a picture that we've realized we're lost,

910
00:56:03,520 --> 00:56:04,640
that we're walking our own way.

911
00:56:04,640 --> 00:56:08,320
It's a visible symbol that we've repented

912
00:56:08,320 --> 00:56:10,080
and we are willing to die to our own self

913
00:56:10,080 --> 00:56:11,420
and submit our life to Jesus.

914
00:56:11,420 --> 00:56:15,300
Baptism is done by guides along the way.

915
00:56:19,300 --> 00:56:21,360
I love, again, we'll read Romans 6 one more time

916
00:56:21,360 --> 00:56:21,800
as we're ending.

917
00:56:21,800 --> 00:56:23,740
Welcome, children.

918
00:56:23,740 --> 00:56:25,300
How are we?

919
00:56:25,300 --> 00:56:26,660
Good.

920
00:56:26,660 --> 00:56:29,640
I preached for a long time.

921
00:56:29,640 --> 00:56:30,400
I'm so sorry.

922
00:56:30,400 --> 00:56:30,880
All right.

923
00:56:30,880 --> 00:56:32,140
Romans 6.

924
00:56:32,140 --> 00:56:33,820
Don't you know that all of us

925
00:56:33,820 --> 00:56:35,120
who were baptized into Christ

926
00:56:35,120 --> 00:56:37,060
were baptized into his death.

927
00:56:37,060 --> 00:56:38,540
We therefore buried with him

928
00:56:38,540 --> 00:56:39,820
through baptism into death

929
00:56:39,820 --> 00:56:43,000
in order that just as Jesus was raised from the dead

930
00:56:43,000 --> 00:56:43,980
through the glory of the Father,

931
00:56:44,100 --> 00:56:46,740
we may to live a new life.

932
00:56:46,740 --> 00:56:49,160
Multiple people have pre-decided

933
00:56:49,160 --> 00:56:51,060
that they're going to make that decision this morning

934
00:56:51,060 --> 00:56:51,760
if you're in here

935
00:56:51,760 --> 00:56:53,720
and you have not yet made that decision.

936
00:56:53,720 --> 00:56:55,400
There are towels.

937
00:56:55,400 --> 00:56:56,760
There are clothes.

938
00:56:56,760 --> 00:56:59,320
We would love to celebrate this with you.

939
00:57:00,240 --> 00:57:01,700
Please, as we sing,

940
00:57:01,700 --> 00:57:04,140
consider whether or not

941
00:57:04,140 --> 00:57:06,620
today might be the day

942
00:57:06,620 --> 00:57:08,180
that God gets your attention

943
00:57:08,180 --> 00:57:09,560
and that you turn from the wide road

944
00:57:09,560 --> 00:57:10,500
that leads to destruction

945
00:57:10,500 --> 00:57:11,960
back to the narrow road

946
00:57:11,960 --> 00:57:12,680
that leads to life.

947
00:57:12,680 --> 00:57:13,080
Let's pray.

948
00:57:13,080 --> 00:57:14,360
Father, we are so thankful

949
00:57:14,360 --> 00:57:15,620
for this morning

950
00:57:15,620 --> 00:57:17,020
to celebrate these decisions.

951
00:57:17,020 --> 00:57:18,740
We're so thankful,

952
00:57:18,740 --> 00:57:20,900
God, that you love us enough

953
00:57:20,900 --> 00:57:21,920
to confront us

954
00:57:21,920 --> 00:57:23,740
in our own direction,

955
00:57:23,740 --> 00:57:24,840
in our own way,

956
00:57:24,840 --> 00:57:26,300
that you wake us up

957
00:57:26,300 --> 00:57:27,000
from the death,

958
00:57:28,660 --> 00:57:30,260
the sin that leads to death,

959
00:57:30,260 --> 00:57:31,760
and you turn us around

960
00:57:31,760 --> 00:57:33,780
to obedience that leads to life.

961
00:57:33,780 --> 00:57:36,680
God, may we be a people

962
00:57:36,680 --> 00:57:37,420
who are known

963
00:57:37,420 --> 00:57:39,440
for the direction of our lives.

964
00:57:39,440 --> 00:57:41,740
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

965
00:57:41,740 --> 00:57:42,420
Amen.

966
00:57:42,420 --> 00:57:43,800
All right.
